    "standardized_narrative": "During 2021 the syndicate recognised favourable prior-year development, with a reported surplus of GBP 33.737m relating to reassessment of net claims for previous accident years (a release). This release was driven by benign attritional claims and favourable reserve reviews across multiple classes, although the 2019 year of account had been adversely impacted by COVID-19 related event cancellation and trade interruption losses and by Storm Dorian and subsequent tornado events. The calendar year also experienced several 2021 catastrophe events (notably Hurricane Ida and Winter Storm Uri) which impacted current year claims but did not offset the prior-year reserve releases.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "Within the calendar year technical result, a surplus of GBP 33,737,000 (2020: surplus GBP 51,972,000) relates to the reassessment of net claims incurred for previous accident years.",
      "reserve releases across most other classes given favourable historic claims experience.",
      "The underwriting loss was predominantly driven by significant COVID-19 losses through its exposures to event cancellation and trade interruption risks within the Contingency and Property classes respectively.",
      "The syndicate has maintained its prudent approach to reserving with initial reserves being set to include a margin that is expected to release over time as uncertainty reduces."
